# Commander front battery bar (rev S0) - BMS board, microcontroller and the ports.
#
# STC8H8K64U (the keyboard's and the internal battery's chip: one part number, one tool chain), at 3.3 V.  It is the
# bar's gauge and charge controller, and a USB HID "Power Device" (UPS class) towards the terminal, exactly like the
# internal battery module (commander_battery), so the terminal's software sees either of them the same way.
#
# Two ports, wired in parallel (only one is used at a time):
#   J1  USB-C receptacle on the bar's left end face: charge the bar from any USB charger, use it as a power bank, or
#       cable it to the terminal's battery port J40;
#   J4  the dock: a 5-way harness to the bar's docking contacts (INPUT_MODULE_CONNECTOR of the chassis model), so the
#       bar powers the terminal when it is clipped on, without a cable.
# The port role is the internal module's: Rp (36 k to 3.3 V) by default = "I am a source"; Rd switched in when the
# terminal asks for a charge (HID feature report).  See README.md.
SHEET bar_mcu

U1 STC8H_LQFP32:STC8H8K64U 10=VCC3V3 11=VCC3V3 12=GND
P U1 8=UCAP 13=USB_MCU_DM 14=USB_MCU_DP 15=BTN_N
# analogue inputs: ADC0, ADC1, ADC3 (strings), ADC4 (pack current), ADC5 (charge current), ADC6 (port), ADC7 (solar),
# ADC8-ADC10 (thermistors), ADC11 (the pack current sense's zero, for calibration)
P U1 1=VSTR1_ADC 2=VSTR2_ADC 7=VSTR3_ADC 3=IPACK 4=ICHG 5=VBUS_ADC 6=SOLAR_ADC
P U1 29=NTC1 30=NTC2 31=NTC3 32=ISNS_REF
# control: charger enable, charge set point (PWM6 of PWMB on P2.1), buck off, port role, fuel LEDs, string switches,
# port-to-charger switch
P U1 21=CHG_EN 22=CHG_PWM 23=OUT_OFF 24=CC_RD 25=CC_RP 26=LED1_K 27=LED2_K 28=LED3_K
P U1 16=CHG1_EN 17=CHG2_EN 18=CHG3_EN 19=USB_CHG_EN
NC U1 9 20
C40 1uF UCAP GND
C41 100nF VCC3V3 GND
C42 100nF VCC3V3 GND
C43 4.7uF VCC3V3 GND

# button (side-operated, behind the left end face): press = show the charge; held while plugging in = STC boot loader
SW1 TACT_SIDE:BTN 1=BTN_N 2=GND
R40 10K VCC3V3 BTN_N

# fuel LEDs (25 / 50 / 75 %), sunk by the microcontroller; seen through light pipes in the left end cap
R50 1K VCC3V3 LED1_A
D50 LED:GREEN A=LED1_A K=LED1_K
R51 1K VCC3V3 LED2_A
D51 LED:GREEN A=LED2_A K=LED2_K
R52 1K VCC3V3 LED3_A
D52 LED:GREEN A=LED3_A K=LED3_K

# --- USB-C port on the bar's end face ---
J1 USBC16 A1=GND A12=GND B1=GND B12=GND SH=GND A4=VBUS A9=VBUS B4=VBUS B9=VBUS
P J1 A5=CC1 B5=CC2 A6=USB_CON_DP B6=USB_CON_DP A7=USB_CON_DM B7=USB_CON_DM
NC J1 A8 B8
U2 USBLC6-2SC6 1=USB_CON_DP 6=USB_CON_DP 3=USB_CON_DM 4=USB_CON_DM 2=GND 5=VBUS
R41 22R USB_CON_DP USB_MCU_DP
R42 22R USB_CON_DM USB_MCU_DM
# role: Rp from CC_RP (driven high = source), Rd switched in by CC_RD (sink); both off with the microcontroller off
R43 36K CC_RP CC1
R44 36K CC_RP CC2
R45 5.1K CC1 CC1_RD
Q3 NMOS_GSD:2N7002 D=CC1_RD S=GND G=CC_RD
R46 5.1K CC2 CC2_RD
Q4 NMOS_GSD:2N7002 D=CC2_RD S=GND G=CC_RD
R47 100K CC_RD GND

# --- dock harness (to the docking contacts on the bar's rear face): VBUS, D+, D-, CC, GND ---
J4 JST_PH5:DOCK 1=VBUS 2=USB_CON_DP 3=USB_CON_DM 4=CC1 5=GND
